From 7a40c79dce35025ef443275f22073e25d62a0462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drmortalwombat <90205530+drmortalwombat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:41:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/32] Fix array in array index const folding

(cherry picked from commit 1ae3216fa3699465746fa8fd8e09617f7b8c742a)

Backport to v1.32.273 for nethack64.  The Declaration.cpp change applies
as is: Expression::ConstantDereference returned the initializer's element
declaration itself, whose mOffset is the element's offset inside the
aggregate, and the code generator adds a constant pointer's mOffset to
the pointer.  A pointer read from a const table at a constant index k, or
as a struct member at a non zero offset, pointed that many bytes past its
target.  The element is now cloned and its offset cleared.

Left out: the upstream commit's other hunk, which only changes the
debugging define CHECK_FUNC in InterCode.cpp; it stays at its v1.32.273
value.
---
 oscar64/Declaration.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/oscar64/Declaration.cpp b/oscar64/Declaration.cpp
index d5669c5..240ef94 100644
--- a/oscar64/Declaration.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/Declaration.cpp
@@ -634,6 +634,9 @@ Expression* Expression::ConstantDereference(Errors* errors, LinkerSection* dataS
 					else
 					{
 						Expression* ex = new Expression(mLocation, EX_CONSTANT);
+						mdec = mdec->Clone();
+						mdec->mOffset = 0;
+
 						ex->mDecValue = mdec;
 						ex->mDecType = mDecType;
 						return ex;
